chore(ci): gate patch-script recipes in repo text

AGENTS.md "Editing Discipline" binds every prompt and skill body authored
here, but it is prose, so nothing stopped an example from shipping the
recipe anyway. scripts/check-editing-discipline.py scans the text surfaces
this repo owns (AGENTS.md, docs/, .omp/, .claude/, crates/*/README.md) and
reports five forms that rewrite a tracked file from a shell: sed -i and
--in-place, perl -pi -e, an interpreter heredoc (python/perl/ruby/node,
any version suffix), an ed or ex script, and awk or tee redirected over a
source path. It fails with the file, line and form.

Two escapes carry a reason: an editing-discipline-allow marker, and a fence
opened as a text prohibited block. The rule's own section in AGENTS.md is
skipped by heading so it may quote what it forbids; if that heading is
renamed the skip simply stops applying, so the section's own examples get
reported rather than the rest of the file being swallowed.

Wired into just lint and the CI format job. Proven by planting each form in
a scratch doc: all are reported, exit 1, and the tree is clean again once
removed. One pre-existing hit is marked rather than rewritten, because it
names omp's own sed/jq builtins, not an edit recipe.

Also rewrites the remote_seed job's if: from a folded block wrapping an
expression to a plain expression. actionlint flags the folded form as
always true, because the value carries characters outside the ${{ }}; a
review disputed that reading, citing that if: is evaluated as an expression
regardless. The plain form is unambiguous either way, so this is a
clarity change and not a verified security fix.